{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.AxialCoupling","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AxialCoupling","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnot","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecay","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeH3","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SymmetricIdempotent"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.color_avg_essential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.color_avg_essential","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AxialCoupling.lean#L212-L232","doc":"The 3-fold color average is essential: no single pairing\ngives the correct g_A.\n\n- h₀₁ alone: tr_std/tr_sym ≈ 0.59 → g_A ≈ 0.98 (−23%)\n- h₀₂ alone: tr_std/tr_sym ≈ 1.12 → g_A ≈ 1.86 (+46%)\n- ⅓(h₀₁+h₁₂+h₀₂): tr_std/tr_sym ≈ 0.766 → g_A ≈ 1.277 (+0.1%)\n\n**Scope (owner ruling 2026-11-15, PR #7823).** Keeping the 3-fold average because it\nlands at +0.1 % against PDG is a selection against the target, i.e. a fit under the\nNO-FITTING directive, and the `5/3` prefactor is imported from the naive quark model.\n`g_A` is therefore NOT derived; see `observations/hadron-half-life-verification.md`,\nitem 3. This theorem proves only that two traced volumes differ.\n\nFormally: the color-averaged traced volume differs from each\nindividual half-Borromean traced volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.std_trace_braid_dependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.std_trace_braid_dependent","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AxialCoupling.lean#L175-L209","doc":"The standard trace DOES depend on the specific braid topology.\nThis is the source of the g_A suppression: the standard (2D)\nrepresentation distinguishes different braid structures.\n\nFormally: there exist two Hecke elements with the same total\nσ-count but different standard traces. Witnessed computationally\nby `h₀₁` vs `h₁₂` in the axial coupling calculation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.sym_trace_ordering_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.sym_trace_ordering_independent","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AxialCoupling.lean#L163-L173","doc":"Per-instance form: ordering-independence on the symmetric\nchannel, with the `InSymmetricIdempotent` hypotheses making the\nuniversal-quantifier defect of the earlier axiom explicit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.symCharacterEqual_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.symCharacterEqual_refl","kind":"instance","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AxialCoupling.lean#L158-L161","doc":"Reflexivity instance: when `x = y` syntactically, the cleared\ntraces are equal by `rfl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SymCharacterEqual.cleared_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SymCharacterEqual.cleared_eq","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AxialCoupling.lean#L156-L156","doc":"Cleared traces agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SymCharacterEqual.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SymCharacterEqual.mk","kind":"ctor","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AxialCoupling.lean#L154-L154","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SymCharacterEqual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SymCharacterEqual","kind":"class","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AxialCoupling.lean#L150-L156","doc":"Symmetric-character equality witness — per-pair.\n`SymCharacterEqual x y` records that `x` and `y` have the same\nsymmetric-character value, which by Murphy's theorem implies\ncleared-trace equality once both factor through `e_{(n)}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.InSymmetricIdempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.InSymmetricIdempotent","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AxialCoupling.lean#L117-L134","doc":"**Symmetric-idempotent factorisation predicate.**\nA `TMatrix` `x` factors through the symmetric Young idempotent\n`e_{(n)}` if it admits the form `x = e_{(n)} · b · e_{(n)}` for\nsome Hecke element `b`. By Murphy/Mathas 1992, every such `x`\nhas `tracedVolCleared x` determined by the σ-exponent sum\nalone (the symmetric character `χ(b) = ∏ⱼ (q · cⱼ + dⱼ)`\ndepends on the multiset of crossing coefficients but not on\ntheir ordering).\n\nTreated as a per-element predicate (so call sites supply the\nfactorisation witness) rather than an opaque structural fact.\n\nRe-exported from `QOU.Mathlib.SymmetricIdempotent` (Murphy/Mathas\nupstream); concrete definition is the existential\n`∃ b, tracedVolCleared x = tracedVolCleared b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.axialCouplingRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.axialCouplingRatio","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AxialCoupling.lean#L80-L99","doc":"The axial-vector coupling ratio as an element of the\nfraction field of `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`.\n\n`g_A(q) = (5/3) × |tr_std(β_color)| / |tr_sym(β_color)|`\n\nwhere `β_color = ⅓Σ h_ij` is the 3-fold color average.\n\nThe factor `5/3` is the naive quark model prediction\n(SU(6) symmetry).  The ratio of irrep traces is the\nq-deformation correction.\n\n**Geometric meaning**: ratio of transverse (axial/standard)\nto longitudinal (vector/symmetric) fiber action of the\ncolor-averaged Borromean topology on `Σ₄`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.borromeanColorAvg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.borromeanColorAvg","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AxialCoupling.lean#L66-L76","doc":"The 3-fold color average of the half-Borromean:\n`⅓(h₀₁ + h₁₂ + h₀₂)`.\n\nThis averages over the 3 cyclic orderings of the quark\ncolors `(r,g,b)` within the nucleon's Borromean triple.\nEach ordering sees a different fiber anisotropy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromean","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AxialCoupling.lean#L49-L62","doc":"The half-Borromean braid `h_{ij} = σ_i⁻¹ σ_j σ_i σ_j⁻¹` in `H₃(q)`.\n\nThis is a 4-crossing element that generates the Borromean\nlinking between strands `i` and `j` (with strand `k` as the\nspectator).  It is NOT the full Borromean link — the full link\nrequires the 3-fold color average.\n\nOver `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`: `σ⁻¹ = σ - (t² - t⁻²)` (Hecke relation). ","signatureChunk":0}]}